    "updated_at": "2017-01-24T14:57:43Z",
    "body": "The spec's first step for `Worker` constructor says\r\n\r\n> The user agent may throw a \"SecurityError\" DOMException and abort these steps if the request violates a policy decision (e.g. if the user agent is configured to not allow the page to start dedicated workers).\r\n\r\nbut it's unclear to me it is a good idea to have these tests pass if a `SecurityError` is raised. In Chromium it seems `SecurityError` is raised for cross-origin URLs, but that is not really per spec (since the URL has not been parsed yet in the spec).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
